@startuml getLogicalTerminationPointListAsync
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title
getLogicalTerminationPointListAsync – Retrieve Logical Termination Points (optionally filtered by layerProtocolName)
end title

participant "requestor" as requestor
participant "ControlConstruct" as ccRes #LightCyan
participant "JSON Driver" as jd #LightYellow
participant "config.json" as cfg #LightGrey

note over requestor
  - layerProtocolName(optional)
end note

requestor -> ccRes: (layerProtocolName)
activate ccRes

ccRes -> jd: read logical-termination-points
activate jd

jd <-> cfg: retrieve control-construct
jd --> ccRes: list of LTPs
deactivate jd

note over ccRes
  <u>Processing</u>
  - If layerProtocolName is provided:
     * Filter LTPs where layer-protocol-name
     matches layerProtocolName
  - Else:
     * Return all LTPs
  - Return array of LTP objects
  - Return empty array if no matching LTPs exist
end note

ccRes --> requestor: Array of LTP objects | []
deactivate ccRes

@enduml
